// Component Observe of the agency context (dhf/spec/model.edn,
// :agency/observe; dhf/spec/07-measure/observe.feature): the task "rdm-spec
// observe begin CYCLE ROLE ROOM, or end CYCLE ROLE [--tokens N], or report
// CYCLE CYCLE", which records each run's time, cost and defence (what it
// touched outside its room) into dhf/cycles/CYCLE/runs.edn, and sets two
// cycles' runs side by side, never netted (the glossary's "Run",
// "Observation" and "Breach"). It observes from outside: it records, never
// prevents, never stops a run; reads are not observed, and the record says
// so.
//
// The watched directories (the configuration's :agency :watch, "~" the home
// directory) and the temporary directory (:agency :tmp) lie outside the
// project: they are read through the host's standard interfaces from the
// root folder the host opens (slice 01's ED-05), the home directory from
// the environment the host passes (dhf/spec/07-measure/decisions.md, ED-02).
// The project's git status, outside the cycle, is read by running git
// through rdm:host/process in the project's root, on the project's folder
// within its repository (ED-10). What begin saw is kept in the cycle's
// directory until end reads it (ED-08). Its types are its own and builtin.

interface agency-observe {
    /// What the task did, as tasks' outcome (tasks.wit) in this interface's
    /// own types: exit, standard output (the result as EDN), error lines
    /// (each write outside the room a warning naming it, spec-0287).
    record outcome {
        exit: u8,
        stdout: string,
        errors: list<string>,
    }

    /// A run's defence (spec-0286): the paths written outside its room in
    /// the watched directories (spec-0287), the entries it left in the
    /// temporary directory (spec-0288), the project's paths it changed
    /// outside its cycle, relative to the project's folder (spec-0289),
    /// whether the configured results directory was written inside its room
    /// (spec-0290), and what could not be observed, reads outside the room
    /// always among them (spec-0291; G-32).
    record defence {
        writes-outside: list<string>,
        tmp-left: u32,
        repo-touched: list<string>,
        results-in-room: bool,
        unobserved: list<string>,
    }

    /// One entry of runs.edn (spec-0286): exactly :role, :room, :began,
    /// :ended, :minutes, :tokens and :defence (G-31 for each one's form).
    record run-entry {
        role: string,
        room: string,
        began: string,
        ended: string,
        minutes: f64,
        tokens: option<u64>,
        defence: defence,
    }

    /// Runs "rdm-spec observe begin CYCLE ROLE ROOM", "observe end CYCLE
    /// ROLE [--tokens N]" or "observe report CYCLE CYCLE" with its
    /// arguments, as given, and the project's folder (tasks.wit, request).
    /// begin records what the run starts from (ED-08); end compares, appends
    /// one entry to runs.edn, warns of each write outside the room and exits
    /// 0 (spec-0287), and with no begun run of the role in the cycle exits 2
    /// saying so (spec-0292); report prints {:observe {:cycles :runs
    /// :minutes :tokens :breaches}} (spec-0293; G-38).
    run: async func(args: list<string>, folder: option<string>) -> outcome;
}

/// The component agency/observe builds to: it lists directories and reads
/// the clock through the host's standard interfaces, and runs git through
/// the host. Its standard interfaces are those every component carries, in
/// the version slice 01's worlds name (slice 02's ED-08; ED-12).
world agency-observe-component {
    import rdm:host/process@0.1.0;
    export agency-observe;
}
